WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Your first summer job pays out,

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.900
and your income jumps.

3
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.670
Suddenly you're eating out more,

4
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:07.520
and buying more clothes.

5
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.520
But the instant noodles you lived on?

6
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.680
You buy fewer packs than before.

7
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.050
More money, less of something.

8
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:17.870
When people get richer, why do
they buy less of some things?

9
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:20.780
In this mission, you'll move
an income slider and watch

10
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.880
two demand curves respond.

11
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.080
Then you'll see how a price cut on game

12
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.750
consoles can move demand for
a completely different good.

13
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.760
Your mission: figure out why
more income can mean less demand.
